1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:17,220
Summer has come again this year

2
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,900
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here

3
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,160
Summer has come again this year

4
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,360
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here

5
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,620
On the big road,
drinking till we're dry, camping out

6
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:31,540
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here

7
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:34,580
With big chests, chest to chest,
eating while camping out

8
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,080
Nagisa Club

9
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,820
Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle, jiggle,
jiggle, jiggle, jiggle, jiggle

10
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:40,960
Summer has come again this year

11
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,680
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here

12
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,860
Summer has come again this year

13
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:52,420
Big waves, small waves,
tiny little ones, about this size

14
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,320
Come on the southern wind

15
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,620
Big bottoms, small bottoms,
tiny little ones, about this size

16
00:00:58,620 --> 00:00:59,640
Even just me

17
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:20,660
Perish on the shore, perish on the shore,
perish-ri on the shore.

18
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,440
Booming business! A flying food stall!

19
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,220
What on earth is this?

20
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:43,860
A request for a talk?

21
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:44,300
Yes.

22
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,100
Are you giving up on the talk, senior?

23
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,740
Come on, Chief.

24
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:54,100
Please read it as a leave request.

25
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,160
A leave request?

26
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:57,760
Idiot!

27
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:01,280
A grown man who can't
even write kanji properly!

28
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,820
If you're taking a leave,

29
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:04,720
are you going on a blind date or something?

30
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:05,460
No way.

31
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:09,540
The reason is written in detail inside.

32
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:19,220
Leave request for viewing the fireworks festival.
Ryotsu Kankichi

33
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:25,020
Ever since I was a kid, I've had a
real weakness for fireworks festivals.

34
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:27,120
Idiot!

35
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:31,640
Do you even understand what job you have?

36
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:33,980
Of course, I'm a police officer!

37
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:39,340
Do you think a police officer should be
allowed to take leave for a fireworks festival?

38
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,780
The fireworks festival always draws a huge crowd,
you know.

39
00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:45,600
We're so short-staffed on security
that we'd take even a cat's paw.

40
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,501
Well, your stroke technique

41
00:02:48,551 --> 00:02:50,880
Should I just go AWOL?

42
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,760
If you did that, you'd be fired on the spot!

43
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:56,220
Just kidding, just kidding.

44
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:06,240
The chief's stubborn head works
me to the bone every single day.

45
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:06,620
Tch...

46
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:12,080
Watching the fireworks from
atop that would be the best

47
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:13,940
Damn it!

48
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,280
I wish there were some way
to take a day off easily.

49
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:18,380
Hey!

50
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,480
Ryo-san!

51
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:21,540
Ryo...

52
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,760
Eek!

53
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:24,240
No!

54
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,360
You've got a tab built up, you know!

55
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,940
I-I was just about to pay you back!

56
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,180
Hehehehehe

57
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:30,080
Yeah!

58
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,140
Hahahahaha

59
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,380
I can't pay what I don't have, though!

60
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:34,880
Hehehe

61
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,820
Is business really that bad?

62
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,400
Even if Ryo-san paid off our tab,

63
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,900
it'd be like pouring water on hot stones.

64
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,240
We're one step away from that.

65
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,980
Huge condos are going up everywhere,

66
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,820
so aren't more people eating ramen now?

67
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:02,700
In those high-rises,
nobody can even hear the chalumeau horn.

68
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,900
Why not just do deliveries?

69
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,200
You've got a phone, after all.

70
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:10,180
No way, I'm alone here.

71
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:11,960
Pulling the cart along

72
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,840
can't exactly ride the elevator, can I?

73
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:15,960
Delivering by helicopter

74
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,280
would cost far too much.

75
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,060
Plus, the engine noise is loud.

76
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,540
Something more convenient...

77
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,720
So they're up and running

78
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,500
Katsushika Balloon Club.

79
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,380
Ryo-san.

80
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:55,040
Did this balloon get nervous or something?

81
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,140
I borrowed money, you see.

82
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,380
The old ones,

83
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,560
they're just stuffed in the storehouse.

84
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,900
Would you mind lending
one to me if you don't mind?

85
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:05,720
A friend of mine is interested, so...

86
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,660
We'd welcome any new members with open arms!

87
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,000
Go right ahead.

88
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,760
You want to ride this
thing and make deliveries?

89
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:25,320
We can use the propane
gas for fuel too, right?

90
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,020
So we make ramen inside it?

91
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:29,880
What do you think?

92
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:34,320
Looks like he's totally taken with it.

93
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:42,620
Well, I don't know... Yes, please. Right,
then let's give it a test flight right away.

94
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:52,020
It's inflating. Remember the steps.

95
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:57,660
Tonight, the two of us will be piloting it,
so pay attention.

96
00:05:57,660 --> 00:06:01,000
Eeeeeh?
Don't go asking that hairy guy for help!

97
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,180
Don't you think so? I heard they're
running a food stall in a hot air balloon.

98
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,660
I think they'd gladly cooperate.

99
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:15,960
Night balloon flights aren't permitted in Japan, you know.
So if the guy from downtown finds out about this plan...

100
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:22,400
Once he gets angry, he's scary.
We might get killed, you know, seriously.

101
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:28,160
Ryo-san and the rest of you, get on quick!

102
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,480
Alright!

103
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:32,100
Calm down.

104
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:35,780
We're flying, we're flying!

105
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:39,100
As expected of a pro, what masterful skill.

106
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:43,880
You control the basic movements of
the hot air balloon with this burner.

107
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,440
It can climb quite high,

108
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:48,860
but we don't need to fly that high.

109
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:50,920
Just up to the height of
the high-rise condominiums.

110
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,080
No, it's nothing.

111
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:58,380
You can also vent hot air when
you want to descend quickly.

112
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:01,000
When you vent the hot air,

113
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,380
You're keen, aren't you.

114
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,440
After all, our livelihood depends on it.

115
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:06,700
Livelihood?

116
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:11,180
Well, this guy wants to
become a hot-air balloon pro,

117
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:18,000
he even wrote in his elementary school essay
that he wanted a career flying through the sky.

118
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,020
Yes.

119
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:21,700
That's reassuring.

120
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,860
I'll train you thoroughly.

121
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:25,380
Thank you in advance.

122
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,880
I'm hungry.

123
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,240
At this hour,
the delivery service is already closed.

124
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:39,280
Ugh, going all the way to the
convenience store is such a pain.

125
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,520
What's that?

126
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,420
What?!

127
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,980
It says "ramen" on it!

128
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:03,000
There's a phone number written here too.

129
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,700
Shall we try calling it?

130
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:14,700
Yes, this is Balloon Ramen.

131
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:15,760
Is that you, friend?

132
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:20,080
Could I get two ramen, please?

133
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:23,440
Two ramen, got it.
And who am I speaking with?

134
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:26,620
It's Yamada, from Room 3011 of Building A.

135
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,320
Room on the 30th floor, right?
Thanks for your order!

136
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,140
We actually managed to place an order!

137
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:34,160
But how are they going to deliver it?

138
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,000
It's coming closer... it's kind of scary.

139
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,560
Thanks for the order!

140
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,720
You're Mr. Yamada, right?

141
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,020
Y-yes!

142
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,640
Here you go, it's ready!

143
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:58,240
That was fast!

144
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:02,300
The inside of the balloon
has turned into a ramen shop!

145
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:03,540
Here you go, thanks!

146
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:04,520
Here you go!

147
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:08,860
Sorry to keep you, that'll be 1,000 yen!

148
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:10,770
Here,

149
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:14,660
Balloon ramen!

150
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:15,932
Here,

151
00:09:15,982 --> 00:09:20,160
Thanks a lot! Three ramen! Beat 40235!

152
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,080
Alright! Amhere, got it!

153
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,240
Got one! Let's move!

154
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:31,620
Another one!

155
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,600
Yes, lots of ramen orders! Thanks!

156
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,440
Chashu ramen, 700 yen!

157
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:40,320
Five miso ramen, got it!

158
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,420
We're swamped.

159
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,980
Ryo-san, there's a patrol car down below.

160
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,520
Someone called 110

161
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:50,700
What do we do?

162
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:53,960
Activate the emergency response formation!

163
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,660
That balloon

164
00:09:58,360 --> 00:09:59,300
Where is it?

165
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,860
It's too dark to see anything!

166
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:03,580
We call it Operation Crow in the Night.

167
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:07,080
That's why we went to the trouble
of painting the balloon black.

168
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,560
Typical, your schemes are the
only thing that never fails you.

169
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:13,900
Most of them get caught by one person.
That's bad for business, you know!

170
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:18,180
Well, I never expected
business to boom like this.

171
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,571
If we keep making money at this rate,

172
00:10:20,621 --> 00:10:23,560
my tab will be wiped clean
as a royalty for the idea.

173
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,897
You're quick to make plans, aren't you.

174
00:10:24,947 --> 00:10:28,240
But is it really okay for a police
officer to moonlight like this?

175
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,304
As a police officer,

176
00:10:30,354 --> 00:10:33,440
it's our duty to lend a hand
to ordinary folks in trouble!

177
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:37,780
If someone's hungry in the middle of the night,
helping them is the right thing to do, isn't it!

178
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:58,600


179
00:10:58,600 --> 00:10:59,600
Maybe it won't come out at all,
don't you think?

180
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:02,300
How do you know that?

181
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,040
That's because the person himself...

182
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:05,480
Ah n-no, no

183
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:09,280
It's what they call a
police officer's instinct.

184
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:12,880
You, with a police officer's instinct?

185
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,060
Such a thing actually exists in you?

186
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,800
Then what will you bet on?

187
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:18,560
Chief, a thousand yen a bet.

188
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:20,140
Idiot!

189
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:22,560
A sacred police officer...

190
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:24,840
Do you think it's okay for them to gamble?

191
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,080
Chief.

192
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,580
Yes, how about this?

193
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:31,680
If Ryo-chan gets a lead
on that suspicious balloon,

194
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,760
how about making the fireworks
festival day our day off?

195
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,360
I see. That's a good idea.

196
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,940
What do you say, Ryotsu?
No complaints, right?

197
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,760
Haha, yeah, right.

198
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:52,320
What a predicament...

199
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:59,380
The beloved summer has arrived.

200
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:02,180
Good work, senior.

201
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:05,060
It's up there, up.

202
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:10,120
What's this? Stargazing on duty?

203
00:12:10,820 --> 00:12:11,980
That's not it.

204
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:15,380
Then what is it?
Can you see even in the dark?

205
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:17,640
Well, just take a peek.

206
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:18,900
A bird?

207
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,540
What, it's a bird!

208
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:27,780
It's so dark, yet you can see it so clearly.

209
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:32,060
It's a starlight scope the US military uses.

210
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,703
If you look through this,

211
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:37,660
you can spot that suspicious
black balloon right away.

212
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:39,800
This is trouble.

213
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:42,740
No, you've gotten hold of something amazing.

214
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,970
If you spot the balloon
together with me, senior,

215
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:47,680
why don't we claim the credit?

216
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:51,100
No, I'll leave the credit to you, junior.

217
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:59,280
Hey, what are you doing here?

218
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,700
Ryo-san.

219
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:04,680
Well, you're always letting
me make money off you, so

220
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,480
I thought I'd bring you
some late-night snacks.

221
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:12,900
Idiot! If you wander around here like this,
you'll look suspicious!

222
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:15,820
The ramen shop!

223
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:19,460
Perfect timing, I was just getting hungry.

224
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:24,380
I've never had yatai ramen before either,
so I'd like to try it.

225
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:27,240
It smells delicious.

226
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:31,580
So this is how a ramen stall is built?

227
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:37,880
That's Mr. Mikura of the Nakagawa conglomerate.
He's a police officer as a hobby.

228
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:40,740
I hardly ever eat ramen, you know.

229
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:43,480
I'm not doing this as a hobby, you know.

230
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:47,680
Speaking of which, that suspicious
balloon was selling ramen too, wasn't it?

231
00:13:50,880 --> 00:13:52,160
The phone's ringing.

232
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,320
Go ahead.

233
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:56,200
Yes, hello, balloon ramen.

234
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:59,080
No, we're just a regular ramen shop.

235
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:02,920
Just a regular ramen shop?

236
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:04,800
You're the balloon ramen place, right?

237
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:07,460
What time tonight will you
be coming around this area?

238
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:09,420
Sorry.

239
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,600
We're closed today.

240
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,560
Yes, thanks,
we look forward to your business again.

241
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:19,060
Aren't you open on your day off?

242
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:20,472
No, well,

243
00:14:20,522 --> 00:14:24,420
I was thinking about knocking
off early tonight too.

244
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:25,940
Hey, Ryo-san.

245
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:29,220
Don't ask me. I don't know anything.

246
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,540
Yeah, that's right.

247
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:42,520
Cat in the air.

248
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,840
Three rotations.

249
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:46,740
It's Ryo-san. I'll open up now.

250
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,860
Whoa! What's with all that stuff?

251
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:54,480
Ramen alone won't bring in much profit,
you know.

252
00:14:55,120 --> 00:15:01,060
Expanding in many directions to meet the needs
of the times is the textbook rule of business.

253
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:02,480
Yeah, yeah.

254
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:09,520
We'll call it a flying convenience store!

255
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:18,700
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for waiting.

256
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,920
Here comes the convenience
store balloon ramen!

257
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:26,180
Yes, here's the convenience
store balloon ramen.

258
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:28,760
Come on, are you coming in?

259
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,820
Here you go, three chashu ramen.

260
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:33,820
Can I get some rice balls too?

261
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:34,840
Sure.

262
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:38,440
Here's the Idol Hell limited edition,
three-volume set.

263
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,020
I really wanted this one.

264
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,320
Hey, could I get an egg?

265
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:43,820
Here you go.

266
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,820
They have everything here, don't they?

267
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,320
Pocky chocolate

268
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,500
Got the Boolong tea and yakisoba,
coming right up.

269
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:52,420
Thanks.

270
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:55,380
They've got coffee to keep you awake, too.

271
00:15:55,820 --> 00:15:56,960
Shaved ice, please.

272
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:01,100
Melon, strawberry,
or condensed milk, which should I get?

273
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,280
Whew, that was a lifesaver.

274
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:06,220
Could I also get two or three
weekly magazines while I'm at it?

275
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,200
Thanks for your business.

276
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:09,500
Too fast, you're going too fast.

277
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,560
This is a huge windfall!

278
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:15,440
Look.

279
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,060
That balloon.

280
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:21,580
Idiot! Right, we're going after it!

281
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:27,060
This is Naocon. We've spotted the
suspicious balloon. Where are you?

282
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:31,420
Okay. Kei-chan,
please get the starlight scope ready.

283
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:32,600
Roger!

284
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:36,880
Well, we really made a killing.

285
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,000
Hello?

286
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:41,700
Sorry. We've already sold out for today.

287
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,700
Here you go.

288
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:47,440
Ryo-san, it's a mini-patrol car!

289
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,340
What!?

290
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,900
That's Komachi and Naoko, isn't it.

291
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:56,680
Alright,
formation against the mini-patrol, launch!

292
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,860
I turned off the lights.

293
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,320
Don't worry,
you look exhausted from the moonlight.

294
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,600
What's that?

295
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,100
It's content.

296
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,000
Hehehe, that's right.

297
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:13,380
This is our secret weapon,
the Mist-or-Hide Operation!

298
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:15,960
Really, you work hard, you rascal.

299
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,920
The moon's disappeared!

300
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:19,920
Smoke!

301
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:22,320
But I can't see the road anymore.

302
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:26,080
Damn it!
Where's the real identity of this thing?

303
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:27,000
I can't see anything!

304
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:30,540
H-hey, wait!

305
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:34,240
Sucker!

306
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,740
I thought I was going to die.

307
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,340
Damn it!

308
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:48,320
Looks like the balloon's heading this way.

309
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,460
But I can't see it at all.

310
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,240
This scope works in the dark, right?

311
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:58,200
It's supposed to see clearly
for several kilometers.

312
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,070
Kei-chan,

313
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,820
this lens -

314
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:05,400
What's wrong?

315
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,100
This is black paint.

316
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,680
Who would do something like this?

317
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:16,400
If you're talking about someone
who'd do something like this,

318
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,960
they're not getting caught that easily!

319
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:22,980
Sorry, Ryo.

320
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,960
making you help out on your day off.

321
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:28,000
You're almost done paying
off your debts, right?

322
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:31,180
Just one more push and you're there.

323
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:34,280
Hey, is this the balloon
ramen convenience store?

324
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,520
I'd like to place an order, please.

325
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,880
That voice here...

326
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,520
It's Ryo-chan after all.

327
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:43,660
You're closing up for
the day already, right?

328
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:44,820
Good night.

329
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:49,980
Right, how did Reiko get
hold of this phone number?

330
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:51,580
No doubt about it.

331
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:56,360
Because that suspicious balloon always
shows up only when Ryo-chan isn't around.

332
00:18:57,980 --> 00:18:58,980
If it's come to this,

333
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,560
that policewoman has caught on to us.

334
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:06,480
Yeah, she's a woman with
a scarily sharp instinct.

335
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:10,300
We'd better wrap things up soon.

336
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,840
Just when we were getting
into the swing of things.

337
00:19:13,580 --> 00:19:13,940
Don't worry.

338
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:17,120
We've got to clear out
this mountain of stock too.

339
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:20,280
Let's make a big score at the end.

340
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,980
If it works out,
you could even own a shop of your own.

341
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:26,960
How are we going to make that kind of money?

342
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,500
We're going to use the fireworks festival.

343
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,600
The fireworks festival?

344
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:34,780
But Ryo-san, can you even take that day off?

345
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,240
A relative of mine has passed away.

346
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,580
Just make up an excuse like
that and you'll get the day off.

347
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:42,900
I've got plenty of elderly relatives,
after all.

348
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:50,360
Chief, actually...

349
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,060
I know, I know.

350
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,540
It's about the leave, right?

351
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,000
Well

352
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,800
I've heard the report.

353
00:19:57,800 --> 00:20:02,940
I hear you've been searching for that
suspicious balloon even on your days off.

354
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:03,840
Ah.

355
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:06,600
For you, that's quite commendable.

356
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:10,020
I'll give you the day off for
tomorrow's fireworks festival, so

357
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:11,660
keep up the investigation.

358
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:12,720
Y-yes, sir.

359
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:15,780
What, you don't seem very happy?

360
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:17,460
Nothing!

361
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:21,700
Suttondororiko sujarakka chanchan sa!

362
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,040
I was really looking forward to the fireworks festival,
you know.

363
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:36,280
And this stakeout with that barbarian...

364
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:38,700
Hey, doesn't this seem a little strange?

365
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:42,460
Those two have been over there
the whole time since earlier,

366
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:48,740
sitting by the window without moving at all?

367
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:50,220
No way.

368
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,600
There's no way I'm letting
Reiko ruin my business!

369
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:59,860
Ryo-san, the time has finally
come to make our grand finale!

370
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:00,380
Yeah.

371
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:05,040
The convenience store balloon ramen's final,
beautiful triumph!

372
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:08,240
Let's light it up like a fireworks show!

373
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:11,000
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for waiting!

374
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,520
The familiar flying convenience store
is here once again!

375
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:15,380
The balloon ramen has arrived!

376
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:18,600
Beer enjoyed while watching the Ido-machi fireworks
,

377
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:20,660
is truly the essence of Japan!

378
00:21:20,660 --> 00:21:23,000
A first-class seat for watching fireworks!

379
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,600
Residents of the high-rise apartments,

380
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:27,080
beer, snacks, and shaved ice,

381
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:29,860
the flying general store
with everything you need,

382
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:31,820
will sell you happiness!

383
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:34,520
All right, everyone, together now!

384
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,780
Come on, all together!

385
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,140
Hey, give me a beer!

386
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:45,200
Can I get some shaved ice!

387
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,980
Yes, sir! Be right with you!

388
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:50,940
Just as I thought!

389
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,260
We got totally played.

390
00:21:57,260 --> 00:22:01,780
Ryo-san! At this rate,
we're gonna sell out of everything!

391
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,380
We're making a killing here, man!

392
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:08,660
What is it? What's wrong?

393
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:11,380
Something's wrong with the balloon,
it's not running right.

394
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:12,780
It's old, after all.

395
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:17,120
It won't stop!

396
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,160
Kei-chan, what about the balloon?

397
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,400
My hunch was right.

398
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:32,480
No doubt about it.

399
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:35,500
So it was Ryotsu after all. This is...

400
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:36,820
You idiot!

401
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:40,600
We're going to crash into the fireworks!

402
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,500
What the hell is this!

403
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:44,020
What the hell is this!

404
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:48,710
Caught up in the fireworks' shockwave,

405
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,840
it looks like it's doing a Dutch roll.

406
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,480
What an unbelievable guy.

407
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:53,820
Ryo-chan.

408
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,320
Is it over?

409
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,680
No, there should still be
a final 15-shell burst left.

410
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,962
It's about 300 meters across,

411
00:23:13,012 --> 00:23:14,620
so if we get caught in it...

412
00:23:14,620 --> 00:23:15,940
Got caught in it?

413
00:23:16,220 --> 00:23:17,620
We're done for!

414
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:29,260
This is the miserable end of a total idiot.

415
00:23:32,600 --> 00:23:33,180
What?

416
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:36,120
Hey! Money's raining
down from the fireworks!

417
00:23:36,540 --> 00:23:37,640
What a show that was!

418
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:40,940
Ryo-san, the money...

419
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:42,661
Well, there's nothing to be done.

420
00:23:42,711 --> 00:23:45,545
We got to see the 15-shell
fireworks up close.

421
00:23:45,595 --> 00:23:48,460
Consider it an admission fee.
I'll give it to everyone.

422
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:05,360
Whoa!

423
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:09,640
I won 5.5 billion yen in a foreign lottery!

424
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,660
That's 5.5 billion yen!

425
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:15,260
I'll pay off my debts,
buy model kits, eat eel and steak!

426
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:17,640
I'll never be able to spend it all!

427
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,940
Next time: "Lottery Jackpot Bastard!"

428
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:21,840
See you then!

429
00:24:33,920 --> 00:24:36,620
Let's smile, okay?

430
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:40,820
Even when something outrageous happens,

431
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:45,340
keep smiling cutely, okay?

432
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:50,560
just head out with a carefree face.

433
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:54,060
Hey, smile for me.

434
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:57,480
It's not your fault.

435
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:02,740
Hey, smile for me.

436
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:07,040
Yeah! Keep up that same energy!

437
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:11,560
Keep smiling at all times, okay?

438
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:16,560
A woman who's too serious isn't beautiful,

439
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:21,340
so she should smile right away.

440
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:25,780
Unless you're a child, that is.

441
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:41,440
Thanks for watching.

